Subject: [PATCH] docs(process): restore the 'Overlapping issues stack' rule
 heading

PR #562's edit to AGENTS.md swallowed the bullet heading of the next
rule, so 'Overlapping issues stack' ran on as part of the fork-sync rule.
The rule's text was intact; this puts its bullet and heading back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 AGENTS.md | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index ecdf585c..adfe8c05 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -125,7 +125,8 @@ go to `CHANGELOG.md`.
     the conflicting upstream change into the branch (`git merge
     upstream/main`) on that branch only, never into the fork's `main`, which
     advances only at the next cut tag.
